From 39fbffaed995bd3c73d3545fd9d94c36a742fcda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 11:57:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0117 -- guard the lone silent GUS_VOICES==28 count

gus_resolve_voices clamped the GUS_VOICES hint only to [14,32]. The value
28 is documented in this file's own header (and in the GUS campaign notes)
as the single dead count: 28 active voices sets the GF1 output rate to
exactly 22050 Hz, which collides with a PicoGUS firmware special-case
(SCALE_22K_TO_44K forces 28-channel output up to 44.1 kHz) while the
driver assumes 22050 -> rate mismatch -> dead silence on g2k. Every other
count in range is audible; 28 is uniquely silent.

The shipped default (20) never hits it, but for a PUBLIC release a stale
autoexec or hand-set SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_VOICES=28 would silently kill
all music with no diagnostic -- a documented hazard with zero code
enforcement. This nudges 28 -> 27 (nearest audible count) and logs a loud
"SDL/0117 GUS-VOICES-GUARD" line explaining why; the nudged count also
shows through the existing SDL/0112 detect banner (voices=/rate=). No new
killswitch: GUS_VOICES itself is the control (any other value is honored).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_gus.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_gus.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_gus.c
index 1447fb233..b4a634734 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_gus.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_gus.c
@@ -596,6 +596,24 @@ static void gus_resolve_voices(void)
     if (v > GUS_MAX_VOICES) {
         v = GUS_MAX_VOICES;
     }
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch 0117 (v1.6.1 public-HW): guard the lone dead voice-count.
+       28 active voices drives the GF1 output rate to exactly 22050 Hz, which
+       collides with a PicoGUS firmware special-case (SCALE_22K_TO_44K forces
+       28-channel output up to 44.1 kHz) while our driver assumes 22050 -> rate
+       mismatch -> dead silence on g2k (see the voice-count/rate note at the top
+       of this file, and gus_campaign_picogus_diag_wedge). Every other count in
+       [14,32] is audible; 28 is the single silent value. The default (20) never
+       hits it, but a hint/stale-autoexec SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_VOICES=28 would
+       silently kill music with no diagnostic. Nudge 28 -> 27 (nearest audible,
+       one extra voice of polyphony vs 27's neighbor) and make it loud so the
+       operator sees why. The resulting count flows into the SDL/0112 detect
+       banner (voices=%d rate=%dHz), so the nudge is visible there too. */
+    if (v == 28) {
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0117 GUS-VOICES-GUARD: requested 28 voices "
+                         "== the PicoGUS 22050Hz/SCALE_22K_TO_44K dead-silence "
+                         "special-case; nudged to 27 (nearest audible count)");
+        v = 27;
+    }
     g_gus_voices = v;
 }
 
